At Sun, 22 Aug 2004 12:25:14 +0900,
Alain Volmat wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> 
> I'm trying to get the dummy (just for a start) driver of alsa-driver 1.0.6
> working on my SH3 Big Endian architecture. My kernel is a 2.4.26 and I got
> problem which I think might come from the memalloc.c part.
> I don't have any PCI on my machine but alsa-driver still want to use
> pci_free_consistent and pci_alloc_consistent and I got a unresolved symbol
> error when trying to load modules:
> 
> modprobe snd-dummy
> /lib/modules/2.4.26-i700-av3/misc/snd-page-alloc.o: unresolved symbol pci_free_consistent
> /lib/modules/2.4.26-i700-av3/misc/snd-page-alloc.o: unresolved symbol pci_alloc_consistent
> /lib/modules/2.4.26-i700-av3/misc/snd-page-alloc.o: insmod /lib/modules/2.4.26-i700-av3/misc/snd-page-alloc.o failed
> /lib/modules/2.4.26-i700-av3/misc/snd-page-alloc.o: insmod snd-dummy failed
> 
> I tried to check a bit the source code but I've to admit that I don't have
> an enough good knowledge of ALSA to understand everything here.

[Added alsa-devel to Cc, which is a better place for such a discussion]

In the recent version, pci_alloc_consistent() is used as a generic
memory allocator, and this looks apparently like a problem in the case
of non-PCI system.

What would be the proper DMA memory allocator functions in the case
without CONFIG_PCI on SH?


Takashi


